menu: the pre-filtered seeding keys two segments: true
menu: each segment offers three or more singles: true
ties: the coarse composite was timed: true
ties: the playoff timed alternates: true
ties: every composite window is the recombination's or the playoff's: true
ties: each faster alternate replaced the incumbent: true
ties: each window differs from the incumbent it challenged in exactly one segment: true
ties: no segment is challenged by more than two windows: true
ties: the crown is the last alternate: true
ties: the crown's time is the last alternate's: true
slower: the playoff timed alternates: true
slower: no slower alternate replaced the incumbent: true
slower: the crown is the recombined composite: true
slower: each window differs from the recombined composite in exactly one segment: true
slower: no segment is challenged by more than two windows: true
near: singles 0.3% apart reach the playoff: true
near: only the single within the margin plays, one per segment: true
spread: the coarse composite was timed: true
spread: singles 1% apart leave the playoff nothing to time: true
wide: the same singles as spread, so only the margin differs: true
wide: a 1.5% margin lets each segment's runner-up 1% behind reach the playoff: true
wide: only the single within the wider margin plays, one per segment: true
off: the reference search played windows a width-0 search must drop: true
off: width 0 times no playoff window: true
off: width 0 times exactly the reference's candidates outside its playoff, in order: true
off: no timing decision is in the playoff phase: true
off: the crown is the recombined composite: true
one: width 1 still plays: true
one: width 1 plays fewer windows than width 2: true
one: no segment is challenged by more than one window: true
trace: one decision per playoff window says phase playoff: true
trace: an unobserved seam reports nothing: true
trace: the same windows, crown and time with the seam observed and unobserved: true
trace: every traced call is one of the search's own, tagged: true
trace: the report counts exactly the traced calls by settle and admission: true
trace: an unobserved search counts as many calls: true
streams: the ambient config leaves both diagnostic streams off: true
log: the logged search adds exactly one decision, last and phase-less (the untuned control): true
log: the report's counts leave out the untuned control, the one untagged call: true
log: the same windows, crown and time with the control on and off: true
log: the scoped search wrote autotune: diagnostics: true
progress: the scoped search wrote one search_start and one search_done: true
progress: the untuned control, under both overrides, wrote its stage line once: true
streams: both overrides end with the search: true
tune_placements: ~log reached its own arm lines, for both arms: true
tune_placements: ~progress framed both arms: true
tune_placements: both arm searches inherited both overrides (an untuned-control stage each): true
streams: both overrides end with the tune_placements call: true
contended: the three searches recombined the same composite: true
contended: the singles tie, so every segment sends two alternates: true
off: no playoff finals ran: true
off: the first segment's slower alternate replaced R, read against R's contended window: true
off: the true best was never timed: true
on: every playoff alternate was a near tie, decided by a finals of the two: true
on: four windows per finals, all admitted: true
on: the first finals is the palindrome of the alternate and R, faster first reading first: true
on: only the true best replaced R: true
on: the true best is crowned: true
on: the playoff's finals windows are not candidate timings or playoff windows: true
on: every playoff window and playoff finals window is in the playoff phase: true
refused: R's finals windows were refused, the alternates' admitted: true
refused: the readings decided R's inconclusive finals, so its first segment was swapped as off: true
refused: the finals' refusals are not the search's: true
